## 🎯 The overall philosophy I'd use

I'd make the game feel like this:

**Early game:**
*"Holy crap, I found a Bulbasaur!"*

**Mid game:**
*"Wait... I can actually find a Dratini here?"*

**Late game:**
*"WHY IS THERE A DRAGONITE IN THIS GRASS?"*

**Power Plant:**
*"Zapdos. ZAPDOS. ZAPDOS. ZAPDOS."*

**Victory Road:**
*"This place is absolutely insane."*

**Cerulean Cave:**
*"Literally anything can happen."*

That gives you a **true hardcore living-dex Kanto**, where every Pokémon has a logical home but you constantly have the possibility of finding something you weren't expecting.

If you're actually implementing this as a ROM hack, the next thing I'd recommend is building a **complete 151-Pokémon master encounter spreadsheet** with columns for **Pokémon → location → encounter % → level range → time/condition → rarity tier → catch difficulty → one-off status**, so you can verify that **all 151 are obtainable without any trades, gifts, or impossible progression requirements.**

